From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:35:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 242/242] ntdll: split the [xp] line's CPU time into user and
 system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The [xp] census's cpu= is ri_user_time plus ri_system_time. In RDR2's
cabin, compressed memory grows from 1.1 to 4.2 GB as the P cores park,
and the time the faulting threads spend in the kernel (page faults,
decompression) hides inside E= (PLA-364, rdr2-cpu-cores §5).

The line now ends with usr= and sys=, the two parts of cpu= in ms over
the tick. Nothing else changes; a release build runs no [xp] sampler
(MADEIRA_NO_DIAGNOSTICS, madeira-unix 0018).

Linear: PLA-364
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-rdr2-kk-audio-diagnostics.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
index 397f917..d6e77f4 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/server_ios.c
@@ -1947,13 +1947,16 @@ static void ios_xprobe_main( void )
             gettimeofday( &tv, NULL ); localtime_r( &tv.tv_sec, &tmv );
             snprintf( wall, sizeof(wall), "%02d:%02d:%02d.%03d", tmv.tm_hour, tmv.tm_min, tmv.tm_sec, (int)(tv.tv_usec / 1000) );
             n = snprintf( line, sizeof(line),
-                          "[xp] %s +%.2f dt=%.0f cpu=%.0f (thr %.0f) P=%.0f E=%.0f run=%.0f pgw=%.1f GHz P=%.2f E=%.2f Minst=%.0f IPC=%.2f mJ=%.0f pin=%llu rdKB=%llu fpMB=%llu",
+                          "[xp] %s +%.2f dt=%.0f cpu=%.0f (thr %.0f) P=%.0f E=%.0f run=%.0f pgw=%.1f GHz P=%.2f E=%.2f Minst=%.0f IPC=%.2f mJ=%.0f pin=%llu rdKB=%llu fpMB=%llu usr=%.0f sys=%.0f",
                           wall, XP_MS( now - t_start ) / 1000.0, dt_ms, cpu, sum_thr_ms, pms, ems,
                           XP_MS( ru.ri_runnable_time - pru.ri_runnable_time ), 0.0 /* Playport: ri_page_wait_time_mach is not in the iOS 26.5 SDK's rusage_info_v6 */,
                           pms > 0 ? pcy / (pms * 1e6) : 0, ems > 0 ? (cy - pcy) / (ems * 1e6) : 0, ins / 1e6, cy > 0 ? ins / cy : 0,
                           (double)(ru.ri_energy_nj - pru.ri_energy_nj) / 1e6,
                           (unsigned long long)(ru.ri_pageins - pru.ri_pageins), (unsigned long long)((ru.ri_diskio_bytesread - pru.ri_diskio_bytesread) >> 10),
-                          (unsigned long long)(ru.ri_phys_footprint >> 20) );
+                          (unsigned long long)(ru.ri_phys_footprint >> 20),
+                          /* Playport (PLA-364): cpu split into user and system time (system: the
+                           * kernel's work for the process, page faults and decompression included) */
+                          XP_MS( ru.ri_user_time - pru.ri_user_time ), XP_MS( ru.ri_system_time - pru.ri_system_time ) );
             if (qf && n < (int)sizeof(line))
                 snprintf( line + n, sizeof(line) - n,
                           " | pres %lld/%lld thr=%.1f ecl %lld/%.1f sig %lld/%.1f wait %lld/%.1f prs=%.1f (flush %.1f lat %lld/%.1f draw %.1f cmt %.1f) pool=%.1f caller-ecl %lld/%.1f",
